    "question": "The pet store can buy a goldfish for $.25 and sell it for $.75. The owner plans to use the profits from goldfish sales to buy a new tank, which costs $100. After one week, he is 45% short of the price. How many goldfish did he sell that week?",
    "gold": "110",
    "answer": "He is $45 short because 100 x .45 = <<100*.45=45>>45\nHe earned $55 off goldfish because 100 - 45 = <<100-45=55>>55\nHe makes $.5 profit per goldfish because .75 - .25 = <<.75-.25=.5>>.5\nHe sold 110 goldfish that week because 55 / .5 = <<55/.5=110>>110\n#### 110"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many goldfish the pet store owner sold in one week, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the profit per goldfish:**\n   The profit per goldfish is the selling price minus the buying price.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Profit per goldfish} = \\$0.75 - \\$0.25 = \\$0.50\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the total amount of money the owner has after one week:**\n   The owner is 45% short of the price of the new tank, which costs \\$100.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Amount of money} = 100 \\times (1 - 0.45) = 100 \\times 0.55 = \\$55\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the number of goldfish sold:**\n   The total amount of money is the profit from selling the goldfish. Since each goldfish yields a profit of \\$0.50, the number of goldfish sold is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of goldfish sold} = \\frac{\\$55}{\\$0.50} = 110\n   \\]\n\nThus, the number of goldfish sold in one week is \\(\\boxed{110}\\).",
